EAST BAY FOUNDERS WEEKLY
Friday, February 27, 2026

Hi all. What's happening for founders in Oakland, Berkeley, Emeryville and Alameda this week.

THIS WEEK
- Demo Night, Thursday March 5, 6:00pm, Jack London Square. Six member companies, five minutes each, no slides over ten. Sign up to present by Monday; there are two slots left. Beer and tacos after.
- Founder Office Hours with two local seed investors, Wednesday 3-5pm at the Temescal space. Twenty-minute slots; book through the member portal.
- The Berkeley hardware meetup is Tuesday at the Marina; not ours, but half of you go.

NEWS
The Uptown coworking space that took over the old bank building on Broadway opens March 16. Founders' Weekly members get the first three months at 20% off; details in the portal. It has a machine shop in the basement, which two of our hardware members have already toured.

The city council voted Tuesday to extend the small-business permit fast track through 2027. If you have been waiting on a sign permit, this is your moment.

MEMBER NEWS
- A member's robotics company closed a large Series C (you know who). Congratulations.
- A B2B payments member is hiring a first sales lead; posting on the job board.
- Two members are looking for a shared office in Alameda; reply and we will connect you.

JOB BOARD: 14 open roles this week, mostly engineering, two in ops, one in sales. https://eastbayfounders.org/jobs

See you Thursday.

